# RULE (SPEC.md §3 / M17's no-I/O refusals; bugs.md 45):
#   A port outside 1..65535 is a MALFORMED ADDRESS and is refused at
#   RemoteLocation::parse(), where every other part of an address is judged, and
#   not carried into a connect. QUrl::port(default) substitutes the default only
#   where the address spells NO port, so an explicit `:0` is a port the address
#   spells and comes back as 0
#
# GUARD: tst_remotelocation::aPortOutsideTheTcpRangeIsARefusedAddressAndNotAFailedConnect
#
# SILENT WHEN BROKEN: `ssh://host:0/path` opens a tab, target() answers
# `user@host:0`, SshSessionCache keys on that string and connectTo() hands the 0
# to a socket. What the user is then shown is a transport error against a machine
# that is up and reachable — the address error reported as though the host had
# refused the connection — with nothing anywhere naming the port as the thing
# that is wrong, and with the M17 refusal that would have named it never reached
# because logPathIsWellFormed() answered true.

diff --git a/src/core/RemoteLocation.cpp b/src/core/RemoteLocation.cpp
--- a/src/core/RemoteLocation.cpp
+++ b/src/core/RemoteLocation.cpp
@@ -148,23 +148,6 @@
         || holdsNoncharacter(loc.path)) {
         return std::nullopt;
     }
-    // A PORT OUT OF RANGE IS A MALFORMED ADDRESS AND IS REFUSED HERE, for the reason
-    // every other range check on an address already is: it is decidable with no I/O
-    // (M17), so it fails the open and names the address, where a port carried through
-    // is reported by the far end as though the host had refused the connection.
-    //
-    // QUrl::port(default) substitutes the default only where the address spells NO port
-    // — `ssh://h/p` and `ssh://h:/p` both answer 22 — so an explicit `:0` is a port the
-    // address spells and comes back as 0, which is not a port: target() answers
-    // `user@host:0`, SshSessionCache keys on it and connectTo() hands it to a socket.
-    //
-    // The lower half is this check's alone. The upper half is Qt's today — `ssh://h:65536/p`
-    // and `ssh://h:-1/p` are already invalid URLs, measured on 6.10 — and it is written
-    // out all the same, because the set of addresses loftail accepts must not be a
-    // function of the Qt build (entry 44's argument, same file): a session file written
-    // against one Qt would otherwise be refused against another. One comparison.
-    if (loc.port < 1 || loc.port > 65535)
-        return std::nullopt;
     return loc;
 }
 
